{"id":"prepositions-0098","taskId":"prepositions","title":"Drill set 98","text":null,"source":"drill","gaps":[{"answer":"after","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Could you look ___ my plants while I\u0027m away?","hint":"look ___ = take care of","explanation":"look AFTER somebody/something = take care of them."},{"answer":"in","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"They arrived ___ Rome at dawn.","hint":"arrive ___ (place), ___ (city)","explanation":"arrive IN towns, cities and countries; AT for buildings/points."},{"answer":"of","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"They accused him ___ lying to the committee.","hint":"accuse sb ___ sth","explanation":"accuse somebody OF something/doing something."},{"answer":"from","accept":["against"],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"Sunscreen protects the skin ___ UV rays.","hint":"protect ___ sth harmful","explanation":"protect somebody/something FROM (or AGAINST) harm."},{"answer":"of","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"I\u0027m sick ___ hearing that song on the radio.","hint":"sick ___ sth (annoyed)","explanation":"sick OF something = fed up with it."},{"answer":"to","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"They\u0027ve invited us ___ their wedding in May.","hint":"invite sb ___ sth","explanation":"invite somebody TO an event."},{"answer":"for","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"We\u0027re hoping ___ the best results this season.","hint":"hope ___ sth (want)","explanation":"hope FOR something = want and expect it."},{"answer":"at","accept":[],"options":[],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"He\u0027s very good ___ solving puzzles.","hint":"good ___ doing","explanation":"good/bad/brilliant AT an activity."}]}